From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Mar 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: rk808: disable boost converter in RK817 syscore shutdown
 to prevent VBUS power-on

On some RK3566 boards (e.g. Miyoo Flip), the USB port generates a
transient voltage on VBUS during system poweroff. The RK817 PMIC
detects this as a charger plug-in event (ON_SOURCE=0x10) and
immediately powers back on, causing the device to reboot instead of
staying off.

The RK817 path does not set device_shutdown_fn, so syscore_ops are
never registered and rk8xx_syscore_shutdown() never runs. The boost
converter stays enabled throughout the entire shutdown sequence,
allowing VBUS transients to trigger PMIC power-on.

Fix this by:
1. Always registering rk8xx_syscore_ops when the PMIC is a system
   power controller (not only when device_shutdown_fn is set).
2. Disabling the boost converter and OTG switch (POWER_EN_REG(3))
   in rk8xx_syscore_shutdown(), right before the SLP pin is set to
   shutdown mode. At this point all device drivers have been stopped,
   so the regulator framework cannot re-enable the boost.

Signed-off-by: Alejandro Corbellini <acorbellini@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/mfd/rk808.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mfd/rk808.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk808.c
@@ -806,6 +806,12 @@
 	 */
 	if (system_state == SYSTEM_POWER_OFF) {
 		if (rk808->variant == RK809_ID || rk808->variant == RK817_ID) {
+			/* Disable boost converter and OTG switch to prevent
+			 * phantom VBUS voltage from triggering an immediate
+			 * PMIC power-on after shutdown.
+			 */
+			regmap_write(rk808->regmap,
+				     RK817_POWER_EN_REG(3), 0x00);
 			ret = regmap_update_bits(rk808->regmap,
 						 RK817_SYS_CFG(3),
 						 RK817_SLPPIN_FUNC_MSK,
@@ -1331,8 +1337,9 @@
 		if (!pm_power_off_prepare)
 			pm_power_off_prepare = rk808->pm_pwroff_prep_fn;

+		register_syscore_ops(&rk808_syscore_ops);
+
 		if (device_shutdown_fn) {
-			register_syscore_ops(&rk808_syscore_ops);
 			/* power off system in the syscore shutdown ! */
 			pm_shutdown = device_shutdown_fn;
 		}
